# FSD for SpexTaxi frontends

Follow Feature-Sliced Design v2.1 (skill: `feature-sliced-design`, doc: `docs/FRONTEND_FSD.md`).

- Next.js: framework routes in package-root `app/`; FSD in `src/_app`, `src/_pages`, later `shared` / `features` / `entities`.
- Expo: framework routes in `src/app/`; FSD in `src/_app`, `src/_pages`, …
- Do not create empty layers. Prefer keeping code in `_pages` until extraction rule holds.
- Do not use `widgets` unless explicitly justified.
- Import only downward; slice public API via `index.ts`.
- Route files stay thin re-exports from `@/_pages/...`.

## Naming

See `docs/NAMING.md`. React component files: **PascalCase** (`HomePage.tsx`).

## Colocation (обязательно)

- One component / function / hook / model = one kebab-case folder.
- Inside: implementation + `*.spec.*` beside it + `index.ts` re-export.
- Segments (`ui/`, `model/`, `api/`) hold unit folders, not flat sibling files.
- Outside the unit, import via its `index.ts` (or the slice `index.ts`).

```text
_pages/home/ui/home-page/
  HomePage.tsx
  HomePage.spec.tsx
  index.ts
```
